# Phase 7 security/hygiene fix: Dockerfile.worker's build CONTEXT is the
# repo root (not ./app — see docker-compose.yml's `worker.build.context`
# and Dockerfile.worker's header comment, since it also needs
# vendor/siteone-crawler/), and the repo root previously had no
# .dockerignore at all. That meant `docker build` sent the ENTIRE repo —
# app/node_modules, app/.next, both .git histories' worth of objects,
# fixtures/node_modules, and critically app/.env (real local secrets in
# a dev checkout) — to the Docker daemon as build context on every
# build. The worker Dockerfile's own COPY instructions are selective
# enough that none of this ever lands in an image layer, but sending a
# real .env file to the daemon at all is unnecessary exposure, and
# node_modules/.git bloat every build's context transfer for no reason.

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
npm-debug.log*
storage/reports
